# Backs the narrow `COPY` enumeration in `docker/Dockerfile` so that
# `docker build` does not silently drag build-context noise into the
# image. `docker/Dockerfile` deliberately lists its build inputs one by
# one rather than running `COPY . .` — a developer's host
# `node_modules/` (built for the host OS/arch) would otherwise clobber
# the just-`npm ci`'d `/app/node_modules`. This file makes the same
# promise on the context side: a stray `COPY . .` introduced by a
# future contributor still won't pull these into the build context.
#
# Keep the file in sync with the explicit `COPY` lines in
# `docker/Dockerfile` — the runtime-stage copy (`/app/dist` →
# `/usr/share/nginx/html`) is unaffected by this list because it uses
# `--from=build`, not the host context.

# Local / CI install outputs — would clobber the `npm ci` step if the
# Dockerfile ever falls back to `COPY . .`.
node_modules

# Build output — the runtime stage pulls `dist` from the build stage
# via `COPY --from=build`, so a context copy would be redundant and
# would also race the build.
dist

# Vite/Sonar/IDE noise that must never enter a build image.
coverage
.vite
.vscode
.DS_Store

# Development-only MSW worker (BSOD-450 moved it here from `public/`). It
# is served by the `team-dash:dev-mock-service-worker` vite plugin during
# `vite serve` only and must never enter a build context.
dev

# Repository history — never needed by the build, and would otherwise be
# exported by `cache-to: type=gha,mode=max` in the release workflow.
.git
.gitignore

# Local environment files. `.gitignore` permits developers to create these;
# they must not reach the daemon or the BuildKit cache.
.env
.env.*

